('math-standard-limits-01','mathematics','calculus','Limits and continuity','Standard limits','What is lim(x→0) sin x/x, with x in radians?','["0","1","−1","does not exist"]',1,'The fundamental trigonometric limit is 1 when angles are measured in radians.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI-XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
